- **Constructor**: It has a constructor that takes a `String` message and passes it to the superclass constructor.

Make sure this class is in the same package (`pacr2`) as your `Rectangle` class, or import it appropriately if it's in a different package.

### Complete Example:
Here is the complete example including the `Rectangle` class and the `BadFigureException` class:

```java
package pacr2;

public class BadFigureException extends Exception {
    public BadFigureException(String message) {
        super(message);
    }
}

package pacr2;

public class Rectangle extends Quadrilateral {

    public Rectangle(String name, Point v1, Point v2, Point v3, Point v4) throws BadFigureException {
        super(name, v1, v2, v3, v4);
        if (!super.isRegular()) {
            throw new BadFigureException("The vertexes are incompatible with a rectangle");
        }
    }

    public double area() {
        Point[] vertices1234 = new Point[] {
            getVertx2(), getVertx3(), getVertx4()
        };

        Point nearestV1 = getVertx1().nearest(vertices1234);

        double distance1 = getVertx1().distanceTwoPoints(nearestV1);

        Point[] otherVertxs = null;

        if (nearestV1.equals(getVertx2())) {
            otherVertxs = new Point[] {
                getVertx3(), getVertx4()
            };
        } else if (nearestV1.equals(getVertx3())) {
            otherVertxs = new Point[] {
                getVertx2(), getVertx4()
            };
        } else if (nearestV1.equals(getVertx4())) {
            otherVertxs = new Point[] {
                getVertx2(), getVertx3()
            };
        }

        Point nearestV2 = getVertx1().nearest(otherVertxs);

        double distance2 = getVertx1().distanceTwoPoints(nearestV2);

        return distance1 * distance2;
