In this corrected version, the `assertEquals` method is used with a precision parameter of `0.000000000000001` to allow for a very small margin of error. This ensures that the test will pass even if there are minor floating-point inaccuracies.

Make sure that the `Point` class has the `distance` method implemented correctly. Here is a possible implementation of the `Point` class:

```java
public class Point {
    private double x;
    private double y;

    public Point(double x, double y) {
        this.x = x;
        this.y = y;
    }

    public double distance() {
        return Math.sqrt(x * x + y * y);
    }
}
