Sure! Let's implement the interactive program to test the `MovementProgrammer` class. The program will read commands from the standard input and perform the corresponding actions.

### TestMovementProgrammer.java
```java
package EjClase;

import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.InputStreamReader;
import java.io.IOException;

public class TestMovementProgrammer {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
        MovementProgrammer programmer = new MovementProgrammer();
        boolean exit = false;
        BufferedReader input = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));

        while (!exit) {
            System.out.print("> ");
            String command = input.readLine();
            if (command != null) {
                String[] parts = command.trim().split("\\s+");
                if (parts.length == 1 && parts[0].equals("exit")) {
                    exit = true;
                } else if (parts.length == 2 && parts[0].equals("displace")) {
                    try {
                        int magnitude = Integer.parseInt(parts[1]);
                        Movement movement = new Movement(Movement.DISPLACEMENT, magnitude);
                        programmer.program(movement);
                        System.out.println("Programmed: " + movement);
                    } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
                        System.out.println("ERROR: invalid magnitude");
                    }
                } else if (parts.length == 2 && parts[0].equals("rotate")) {
                    try {
                        int magnitude = Integer.parseInt(parts[1]);
                        Movement movement = new Movement(Movement.ROTATION, magnitude);
                        programmer.program(movement);
                        System.out.println("Programmed: " + movement);
                    } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
                        System.out.println("ERROR: invalid magnitude");
                    }
                } else if (parts.length == 1 && parts[0].equals("execute")) {
                    Movement movement = programmer.next();
                    if (movement != null) {
                        System.out.println("Executed: " + movement);
                    } else {
                        System.out.println("ERROR: empty movements queue");
                    }
                } else if (parts.length == 1 && parts[0].equals("state")) {
                    System.out.println("Movements remaining: " + programmer.numMovements());
                } else if (parts.length == 1 && parts[0].equals("reset")) {
                    programmer.reset();
                    System.out.println("Movements queue reset");
                } else {
                    System.out.println("ERROR: syntax error");
                }
            } else {
                exit = true;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### Explanation:
- **BufferedReader**: Used to read input from the standard input.
- **Command Parsing**: The input command is split into parts using `split("\\s+")` to handle multiple spaces.
- **Command Handling**:
  - `exit`: Sets the `exit` flag to `true` to terminate the loop.
  - `displace magnitude`: Parses the magnitude and programs a new displacement movement.
  - `rotate magnitude`: Parses the magnitude and programs a new rotation movement.
  - `execute`: Executes the next movement from the queue.
  - `state`: Displays the current number of pending movements.
  - `reset`: Resets the movements queue.
  - Invalid commands: Displays a syntax error message.

### Complete Implementation:
Ensure that all files are correctly implemented and placed in the same package.

### Movement.java
```java
package EjClase;

public class Movement {
    public final static short DISPLACEMENT = 1;
    public final static short ROTATION = 2;
    private short type;
    private int magnitude;

    public Movement(short type, int magnitude) {
        this.type = type;
        this.magnitude = magnitude;
    }

    @Override
    public String toString() {
        if (type == DISPLACEMENT) {
            return "DSP " + magnitude;
        } else if (type == ROTATION) {
            return "ROT " + magnitude;
        } else {
            return "ERR";
        }
    }

    public short getType() {
        return type;
    }

    public int getMagnitude() {
        return magnitude;
    }

    public Movement reverse() {
        return new Movement(type, -magnitude);
    }
}
```

### MovementProgrammer.java
```java
package EjClase;

public class MovementProgrammer {
    private LinkedQueue<Movement> movementsQueue;

    public MovementProgrammer() {
        movementsQueue = new LinkedQueue<>();
    }

    public void program(Movement m) {
        movementsQueue.enqueue(m);
    }

    public Movement next() {
        return movementsQueue.dequeue();
    }

    public int numMovements() {
        return movementsQueue.size();
    }

    public void reset() {
        movementsQueue = new LinkedQueue<>();
    }
}
```

### LinkedQueue.java
```java
package EjClase;

public class LinkedQueue<E> implements Queue<E> {
    private Node<E> top;
    private Node<E> tail;
    private int size;

    public LinkedQueue() {
        top = null;
        tail = null;
        size = 0;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean isEmpty() {
        return (top == null);
    }

    @Override
    public int size() {
        return size;
    }

    @Override
    public void enqueue(E info) {
        Node<E> n = new Node<E>(info, null);
        if (isEmpty()) {
            top = n;
        } else {
            tail.setNext(n);
        }
