Here is an example of how you might define and use a `Point` class in Java:

```java
class Point {
    int x;
    int y;

    // Constructor to initialize the point
    Point(int x, int y) {
        this.x = x;
        this.y = y;
    }

    // Method to display the point
    void display() {
        System.out.println("Point(" + x + ", " + y + ")");
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Declare a variable of type Point
        Point p1;

        // Create an instance of Point and assign it to p1
        p1 = new Point(5, 10);

        // Use the display method to print the point
