### Rational Class

```java
package OOP;

public class Rational {
    // Attributes
    private int numerator;
    private int denominator;

    // Constructor with two arguments (numerator and denominator)
    public Rational(int numerator, int denominator) {
        if (denominator == 0) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Denominator cannot be zero.");
        }
        this.numerator = numerator;
        this.denominator = denominator;
        simplify();
    }

    // Constructor with one argument (integer)
    public Rational(int numerator) {
        this(numerator, 1); // Call the first constructor with denominator as 1
    }

    // Method to simplify the rational number
    private void simplify() {
        int gcd = gcd(numerator, denominator);
        numerator /= gcd;
        denominator /= gcd;
    }

    // Method to calculate the greatest common divisor (GCD)
    private int gcd(int a, int b) {
        while (b != 0) {
            int temp = b;
            b = a % b;
            a = temp;
        }
        return a;
    }

    // Override toString method to display the rational number
    @Override
    public String toString() {
        return numerator + "/" + denominator;
    }
}
```

### TestRational Class

```java
package OOP;

public class TestRational {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Test the first constructor
        Rational r1 = new Rational(3, 4);
        System.out.println("Rational number r1: " + r1); // Expected output: 3/4

        // Test the second constructor
        Rational r2 = new Rational(5);
        System.out.println("Rational number r2: " + r2); // Expected output: 5/1

        // Test simplification
        Rational r3 = new Rational(6, 8);
        System.out.println("Rational number r3: " + r3); // Expected output: 3/4
    }
}
```

### Summary of Changes:
1. **Attributes**: Added `numerator` and `denominator` attributes.
